          "properties": {
            "altText": {
              "expr": {
                "Literal": {
                  "Value": "'Premiere scatter, a static plot of the corrected cut. Horizontal axis: revenue in US dollars on a logarithmic scale. Vertical axis: evidence-weighted rating, with a dashed reference line at the disclosed global mean C = 6.96. Each point is one listing that clears both disclosed bars — a budget of at least $10,000 with revenue above zero, and at least m = 100 votes. The finding: across this population revenue and evidence-weighted quality rise together, and one listing sits highest on both axes at once. Every point is drawn in the same neutral grey; the plot does not colour the winner.'"
                }
